a tsunami brought by the eruption of the  volcano Krakatau has left this coastal  village called lan terra behind me in  Bravos it is in this rubble that a young  father hopes that he will find his  three-month-old baby who has been  missing since Saturday the baby girl's  name is Anissa her body could be  somewhere in this debris fairy Cunha one  of fishermen is her father he lived with  his wife Hannah and their three children  near the water's edge their bamboo hut  couldn't withstand the force of the  giant wave this is all that's left of  our house my mother asked about the  strange sounds outside and when I looked  down I saw three big waves one after the  other I panicked and woke up my wife  we ran out with the whole family this is  where I got hit by the big wave we kept  running over there came the second wave  we fell again and that's when our baby  was torn from my wife's arms we're still  looking for her in this small village of  about 50 residents three people were  unaccounted for two bodies have been  found but ferry and Hannah's baby girl  is still missing in this one behind me  is where Hannah and ferry reunited with  two of their children instead of three  my baby was just wearing the new clothes  I had bought for her she had some new  toys too and she was just starting to  smile and giggle we wanted to go to a  family gathering but when the waves came  I couldn't hold on to her tight enough I  lost her  music thank God the tsunami left Hana  and Ferries family with only the clothes  on their backs and for now all they have  is this picture of Anissa and the hope  that she will be found that report was  sent to us by DW correspondent Anna  Santos and she now joins us from ab one  in western Java which is one of the  worst affected areas Anna we just saw  your heartbreaking report there on that  family praying for a miracle what help  is being provided for those with missing  friends and relatives and aid in general  well families like ferry and Ha